WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.275
Suppose your team is choosing a processor for an embedded controller or a Linux host.

2
00:00:06.275 --> 00:00:08.712
Someone says, “CVA6 supports it.”

3
00:00:08.712 --> 00:00:10.631
What would you check next?

4
00:00:10.631 --> 00:00:14.101
CVA6 is a configurable RISC-V processor family.

5
00:00:14.101 --> 00:00:22.665
Its name alone does not select the instruction set features, memory system or maturity level of your implementation.

6
00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:33.813
In this guide, we will read three real configurations, follow a short execution example, and connect software and application claims to their evidence.

7
00:00:33.813 --> 00:00:43.780
By the end, you should be able to write a useful evaluation statement: which configuration, in which system, supported by which result.

